    "implementedInternalRead": "GET /internal/v1/migration/company-research-parity/{ticker}",
    "behavior": [
      "Spring directly collects current analyst consensus from Yahoo recommendationTrend and financialData instead of reading it from the legacy company projection",
      "the exact megacap batch is AAPL, MSFT, GOOGL, AMZN, NVDA, META, and TSLA with sequential 200 ms pacing and at least three successful tickers",
      "the 0m recommendation trend is preferred and the weighted recommendation score and target-price upside preserve Node rounding",
      "Yahoo cookie and crumb authentication is cached for one hour, invalidated on 401, and never written to logs",
      "a successful direct consensus snapshot is fresh for one hour and usable stale for seven days; failed refreshes do not replace success",
      "all cold requests share one global single-flight batch and non-megacap requests perform no analyst network request",
      "the Node-owned persisted consensus snapshot is used only when the full direct batch is below the minimum success threshold and no usable direct stale exists",
      "per-ticker analyst history remains a read-only Node-owned input and exact 30-day revision calculation remains a pure Java domain policy",
      "source-cache paths, Yahoo transport, cookie handling, JSON parsing, cache state, and sleep pacing remain in outbound adapters",
      "domain and application contain no HTTP, Jackson, filesystem, cache-client, controller, or DTO types",
      "Spring performs no analyst persistence, scheduler, notification, Telegram, or startup network side effect"
